1
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:23,800
Infuriating!

2
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:26,260
This is absolutely vexing!

3
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:35,397
Majesty, you're covered in filth.

4
00:00:35,480 --> 00:00:36,310
What happened to you?

5
00:00:36,393 --> 00:00:38,439
Moreover, where are all the others?

6
00:00:38,960 --> 00:00:39,997
Damn fools.

7
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:44,517
Why did I bother giving them high caliber
weaponry if they don't know how to use it?

8
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:48,377
Majesty, what in heaven is that?

9
00:00:48,460 --> 00:00:52,717
Now that's impossible.

10
00:00:52,800 --> 00:00:56,260
The dragon of calamity.

11
00:00:57,120 --> 00:00:58,200
What is this?

12
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:00,655
The Brio-Lak should have destroyed it!

13
00:01:01,040 --> 00:01:02,160
Could it perhaps?

14
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:04,228
Was it resurrected somehow?

15
00:01:04,860 --> 00:01:06,300
Impossible. No way.

16
00:01:08,120 --> 00:01:10,360
They do have that damn cleric.

17
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:15,380
That infernal healer who can use his
magic far beyond anyone else. Sane.

18
00:01:15,700 --> 00:01:17,600
But even if he did heal it,

19
00:01:17,740 --> 00:01:21,397
it would be impossible for them
to just sick that dragon on me.

20
00:01:21,480 --> 00:01:23,360
Someone must be controlling it.

21
00:01:24,160 --> 00:01:25,320
Demon folk.

22
00:01:27,060 --> 00:01:29,940
Where is our monster person? Pardon?

23
00:01:30,160 --> 00:01:31,840
Where is the Beast Tabor?

24
00:01:32,360 --> 00:01:34,007
Yes, of course, Master Lude.

25
00:01:34,140 --> 00:01:35,777
He has already left for Sorenza.

26
00:01:35,860 --> 00:01:37,477
He spoke of urgent business there.

27
00:01:37,560 --> 00:01:39,137
Of course, that damned Quisling.

28
00:01:39,220 --> 00:01:40,420
Change sides, Azzy.

29
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:44,340
Why did you not try to detain him?

30
00:01:44,620 --> 00:01:48,680
Your Majesty, you told us to give
him special treatment, so I...

31
00:01:51,220 --> 00:01:53,297
My liege, please compose yourself.

32
00:01:53,380 --> 00:01:57,517
I suggest you stop standing around like an
ass and come up with a plan to fix this,

33
00:01:57,600 --> 00:01:59,129
damned good fun of things!

34
00:02:00,740 --> 00:02:01,570
Yes, sire.

35
00:02:01,653 --> 00:02:04,400
Now, get the device ready! The device?

36
00:02:04,860 --> 00:02:06,497
I'm not sure which one you mean.

37
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:08,180
The Koraunos, of course.

38
00:02:08,380 --> 00:02:09,480
The Koraunos?

39
00:02:09,940 --> 00:02:11,440
And be quick about it!

40
00:02:12,000 --> 00:02:15,717
Um, with all due respect, sir, the
Koraunos weapon is still in testing.

41
00:02:15,800 --> 00:02:18,917
Output remains too high and the
sights are unpredictable at best.

42
00:02:19,000 --> 00:02:23,176
And it is wildly dangerous to use
within the city, you wretched coward!

43
00:02:23,820 --> 00:02:26,857
Do you not see the disaster
that is right in front of you?

44
00:02:26,940 --> 00:02:28,097
Yes I do.

45
00:02:28,180 --> 00:02:31,117
But the risk of massive
collateral damage is now.

46
00:02:31,200 --> 00:02:36,737
Do it.

47
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:38,377
We only need one shot.

48
00:02:38,460 --> 00:02:39,377
That is all.

49
00:02:39,460 --> 00:02:40,377
It will take to kill it.

50
00:02:40,460 --> 00:02:43,437
And if you cannot aim it
properly and implement

51
00:02:43,520 --> 00:02:46,917
mana tracing on the gun barrel
right as you command? Sir.

52
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:48,917
You mindless abomination.

53
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:53,180
I'm going to blow you out
of the sky without a trace!

54
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:57,220
Acquiring target, direction 1120.

55
00:02:57,820 --> 00:02:59,940
Angle of fire, 40 degrees.

56
00:03:00,560 --> 00:03:01,795
Mana tracing applied.

57
00:03:06,580 --> 00:03:09,877
Behold the greatest technological
wonder in the Empire!

58
00:03:09,960 --> 00:03:15,260
Developed under the wise leadership
of Doradus III, the Light of Judgment!

59
00:03:18,460 --> 00:03:19,290
Peri!

60
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:26,940
Your Majesty,

61
00:03:27,240 --> 00:03:31,217
the trajectory of Karanos has been
altered and now it's raining down on us!

62
00:03:31,300 --> 00:03:32,130
Talk to me!

63
00:03:32,213 --> 00:03:33,043
How did that happen?

64
00:03:33,126 --> 00:03:35,277
The beam was programmed to trace mana!

65
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:37,477
It's now targeting our mana furnaces!

66
00:03:37,560 --> 00:03:39,457
Why would you ever use
something like that?

67
00:03:39,540 --> 00:03:41,011
Have you no sense at all?

68
00:03:42,980 --> 00:03:44,240
We're all done for!

69
00:03:45,140 --> 00:03:47,280
I'm getting off this merry-go-round!

70
00:03:48,440 --> 00:03:49,840
You are in charge now!

71
00:03:49,940 --> 00:03:51,037
That's a direct order!

72
00:03:51,120 --> 00:03:52,296
Where are you going?

73
00:03:52,540 --> 00:03:53,517
You do something.

74
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:56,129
That is an order from
your direct superior.

75
00:03:59,680 --> 00:04:01,268
It's for the pleasure, sir!

76
00:04:01,600 --> 00:04:02,740
You cowards!

77
00:04:02,880 --> 00:04:04,645
I'll have your heads for this!

78
00:04:10,860 --> 00:04:12,940
Please, no, not those!

79
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:14,320
Anything but those!

80
00:04:14,540 --> 00:04:15,440
Not my babies!

81
00:04:15,720 --> 00:04:17,132
This can't be happening!

82
00:04:20,380 --> 00:04:21,580
Breaking stuff!

83
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:36,577
Let's go to the world.

84
00:04:36,660 --> 00:04:39,484
If you look at me, I'm
going to go to the world.

85
00:04:47,880 --> 00:04:52,280
If you look at me, I can't give up.

86
00:04:54,960 --> 00:04:57,857
What do you want?

87
00:04:57,940 --> 00:05:00,000
What do you want?

88
00:05:28,460 --> 00:05:29,917
Thank you so much for watching.

89
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:03,500
I'm sorry but I seem to
have lost track of him.

90
00:06:03,700 --> 00:06:06,097
I'm trying to pinpoint him but it's as if

91
00:06:06,180 --> 00:06:08,217
there's something
preventing me from doing so.

92
00:06:08,300 --> 00:06:09,476
Then he must be in a

93
00:06:11,760 --> 00:06:13,057
building made of monometal.

94
00:06:13,140 --> 00:06:13,970
Instructor Noor!

95
00:06:14,053 --> 00:06:14,883
Instructor!

96
00:06:18,160 --> 00:06:18,990
Oh!

97
00:06:19,073 --> 00:06:19,903
Um, something's coming.

98
00:06:23,060 --> 00:06:24,957
It's brighter than the light from before!

99
00:06:25,040 --> 00:06:25,870
Fly out of the way!

100
00:06:25,953 --> 00:06:26,783
There's no time!

101
00:06:26,866 --> 00:06:28,500
Everyone, get behind me now!

102
00:06:32,640 --> 00:06:33,800
Instructor!

103
00:06:34,520 --> 00:06:35,460
Perry!

104
00:06:43,700 --> 00:06:44,880
Quill got it!

105
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:46,840
Instructor!

106
00:06:55,280 --> 00:06:56,977
What do you think you're doing?

107
00:06:57,060 --> 00:07:00,917
You were the one who ordered me to come
up with a way to fix this, my liege.

108
00:07:01,000 --> 00:07:01,830
Damn, Tregers.

109
00:07:01,913 --> 00:07:04,457
You do realize this is
treason against the crown?

110
00:07:04,540 --> 00:07:07,337
It is the only way we can
ensure the Empire survive.

111
00:07:07,420 --> 00:07:08,560
No, no, don't.

112
00:07:08,780 --> 00:07:10,980
Someone help me. Seize them.

113
00:07:11,360 --> 00:07:14,497
There is no one here who is
still willing to obey you.

114
00:07:14,580 --> 00:07:15,720
Reap what you sow.

115
00:07:21,940 --> 00:07:22,770
Wow.

116
00:07:22,853 --> 00:07:23,683
Well, that was lucky.

117
00:07:29,380 --> 00:07:31,040
The sparkly gold old guy.

118
00:07:32,200 --> 00:07:33,671
And who the hell are you?

119
00:07:33,760 --> 00:07:35,960
Do you mean to protect this man? No.

120
00:07:36,620 --> 00:07:38,197
Then you need to stay out of our way.

121
00:07:38,280 --> 00:07:40,897
I'm not sure what's going
on, but let's calm down.

122
00:07:40,980 --> 00:07:41,810
Harry!

123
00:07:43,720 --> 00:07:45,340
Old-timer, stay low.

124
00:07:47,500 --> 00:07:49,265
What are you attacking me for?

125
00:07:50,060 --> 00:07:52,001
This man is a seasoned bodyguard.

126
00:07:52,140 --> 00:07:53,337
We must charge together.

127
00:07:53,420 --> 00:07:54,257
This is a misunderstanding.

128
00:07:54,340 --> 00:07:58,516
I see no other way to interpret this
than what is right in front of me!

129
00:07:58,800 --> 00:07:59,630
Perry!

130
00:08:01,140 --> 00:08:04,375
That man has brought irreparable
harm upon our country,

131
00:08:04,560 --> 00:08:07,220
and he must atone for
it with his very life.

132
00:08:07,660 --> 00:08:11,137
I see you guys have some issues,
but can't you just talk it out?

133
00:08:11,220 --> 00:08:13,455
Were that possible, we'd have done it!

134
00:08:14,120 --> 00:08:15,100
Is that a bomb?

135
00:08:15,720 --> 00:08:16,550
Watch out!

136
00:08:22,880 --> 00:08:25,217
Why are you all ganging
up on him like this?

137
00:08:25,300 --> 00:08:26,580
He's just an old man.

138
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,777
You're the one who sent him flying.

139
00:08:28,860 --> 00:08:32,397
Okay, yeah, but isn't he supposed to
be, like, your big emperor or something?

140
00:08:32,480 --> 00:08:34,397
This is all really confusing to me.

141
00:08:34,480 --> 00:08:35,310
That's fine.

142
00:08:35,393 --> 00:08:36,966
You don't need to understand.

143
00:08:37,260 --> 00:08:38,780
Huh? I gotcha.

144
00:08:44,300 --> 00:08:45,337
Could you knock it off?

145
00:08:45,420 --> 00:08:46,250
What is this?

146
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:47,170
What are you doing?

147
00:08:47,253 --> 00:08:48,937
Do you think you can
just kill him yourself?

148
00:08:49,020 --> 00:08:50,857
Of course I'm not going to kill him.

149
00:08:50,940 --> 00:08:51,897
This guy's super old.

150
00:08:51,980 --> 00:08:53,597
He'll probably die any day now.

151
00:08:53,680 --> 00:08:55,057
Let nature do its thing.

152
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:57,493
We do not have a single moment to spare.

153
00:08:57,660 --> 00:08:59,954
Our enemies are invading our territory.

154
00:09:00,240 --> 00:09:03,005
And they have the Dragon
of Calamity with them.

155
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,300
Who's invading?

156
00:09:04,780 --> 00:09:08,877
We need to show them that we have
absolutely no intention of fighting.

157
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:12,019
Our country is doomed unless
we offer them his head.

158
00:09:12,720 --> 00:09:14,380
It is for our survival.

159
00:09:14,920 --> 00:09:16,120
Wait right there.

160
00:09:17,640 --> 00:09:21,758
We appreciate your thoughtfulness,
but there will be no need for that.

161
00:09:22,660 --> 00:09:26,248
For dead men cannot suffer while
they atone for their crimes.

162
00:09:26,440 --> 00:09:27,640
You guys made it.

163
00:09:27,740 --> 00:09:28,570
That's great.

164
00:09:28,653 --> 00:09:29,483
Thanks to you.

165
00:09:29,680 --> 00:09:31,580
And you made it. Yeah.

166
00:09:31,860 --> 00:09:34,777
I thought I was going to eat
it, but I really lucked out.

167
00:09:34,860 --> 00:09:37,200
Are they who I think they are?

168
00:09:37,900 --> 00:09:41,477
Surnar, if you would please, allow
us to take care of things from here.

169
00:09:41,560 --> 00:09:44,957
They're pretty riled up, but I've
been trying to talk them down.

170
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:46,477
Why don't you try giving it a shot?

171
00:09:46,560 --> 00:09:47,972
They won't listen to me.

172
00:09:48,160 --> 00:09:48,990
Thank you.

173
00:09:49,540 --> 00:09:52,716
Lin, could you go with Sir
Noor to tend to his wounds?

174
00:09:53,660 --> 00:09:54,600
Come on, then.

175
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:56,820
Let's get you patched up. Right.

176
00:09:57,180 --> 00:09:58,651
Good luck sorting it out.

177
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:01,670
Now, then.

178
00:10:01,860 --> 00:10:06,620
It has been quite a while since we
last encountered you. Prince Rain!

179
00:10:07,160 --> 00:10:08,917
Please lower your weapons, gentlemen.

180
00:10:09,000 --> 00:10:13,118
and before anything, we would like
to have a discussion with this man.

181
00:10:14,600 --> 00:10:16,700
Please, spare my life.

182
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:18,360
You want to live?

183
00:10:18,660 --> 00:10:21,895
Are you telling me that you
want to receive compassion?

184
00:10:22,240 --> 00:10:23,070
Sure.

185
00:10:23,220 --> 00:10:25,220
I fully intend to forgive you.

186
00:10:25,820 --> 00:10:27,197
Yes? Really? Then I...

187
00:10:27,280 --> 00:10:29,177
There are 23 people in our nation.

188
00:10:29,260 --> 00:10:30,360
Who are missing?

189
00:10:32,320 --> 00:10:35,320
19 people have been buried
under crumbling homes.

190
00:10:35,780 --> 00:10:37,797
13 have been burned to death in fires.

191
00:10:37,880 --> 00:10:40,620
38 people injured by falling debris.

192
00:10:41,660 --> 00:10:44,177
Furthermore, there are
people who were torn apart,

193
00:10:44,260 --> 00:10:46,517
crushed, and reduced to
mangled pieces of flesh?

194
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,247
by the beasts you unleashed.

195
00:10:48,640 --> 00:10:50,660
There are 127 of those.

196
00:10:52,280 --> 00:10:55,960
That total is the number of
casualties in my country.

197
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:59,701
Although I'm certain that
more will be discovered.

198
00:11:00,360 --> 00:11:02,900
Uh, why are you telling me all this?

199
00:11:03,000 --> 00:11:05,840
Because as I said earlier,
I will forgive you.

200
00:11:06,740 --> 00:11:09,997
But only after you have
experienced the same amount

201
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:12,957
of suffering as all those
people I just mentioned,

202
00:11:13,040 --> 00:11:13,870
yes?

203
00:11:16,080 --> 00:11:20,620
Only then will we hold talks about
reparations and ending the war.

204
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,440
What say you?

205
00:11:22,640 --> 00:11:23,875
Are there objections?

206
00:11:24,020 --> 00:11:25,020
No objections.

207
00:11:25,640 --> 00:11:26,680
No, wait, please.

208
00:11:26,900 --> 00:11:28,297
You cannot go through with this.

209
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:30,086
There must be some other way.

210
00:11:30,260 --> 00:11:31,580
No need to worry.

211
00:11:31,860 --> 00:11:34,684
You'll experience their
pain, but you won't die.

212
00:11:35,140 --> 00:11:38,820
Even if we tear off both your
legs and pulverize your innards,

213
00:11:39,600 --> 00:11:42,337
I shall make sure you are
healed enough to survive it.

214
00:11:42,420 --> 00:11:44,380
At least enough to talk to us.

215
00:11:44,940 --> 00:11:46,300
Someone help me!

216
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:50,954
Even if you cannot handle it
and you lose consciousness,

217
00:11:51,080 --> 00:11:52,962
we'll just bring you back again.

218
00:11:53,200 --> 00:11:56,024
Feel free to cry and
scream as much as you like.

219
00:11:57,140 --> 00:11:58,700
Please, I beg you!

220
00:12:00,600 --> 00:12:02,247
Don't get me wrong, Emperor.

221
00:12:03,020 --> 00:12:06,667
However, we're not doing this
because we want to relish in it.

222
00:12:06,820 --> 00:12:10,377
What we do want though
is for you to thoroughly

223
00:12:10,460 --> 00:12:13,813
understand the pain that you
have put our people through.

224
00:12:13,940 --> 00:12:14,770
That's it.

225
00:12:14,860 --> 00:12:17,460
And then you can consider
yourself forgiven.

226
00:12:19,660 --> 00:12:23,131
Because our nation is incredibly
merciful, don't you think?

227
00:12:32,780 --> 00:12:33,860
Ah, thank you.

228
00:12:34,140 --> 00:12:35,817
You are so good at healing stuff.

229
00:12:35,900 --> 00:12:37,380
Ah, thank you. I try.

230
00:12:39,180 --> 00:12:40,300
So much damage.

231
00:12:40,660 --> 00:12:42,677
Did that light from earlier do this?

232
00:12:42,760 --> 00:12:43,920
Yes, it did.

233
00:12:44,300 --> 00:12:47,497
The mana beam that you
deflected was split apart and

234
00:12:47,580 --> 00:12:50,521
then started raining down
on the Imperial Capital.

235
00:12:51,340 --> 00:12:53,517
Oh no, didn't mean for that to happen.

236
00:12:53,600 --> 00:12:55,297
Don't let it bother you, Instructor.

237
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:58,733
You only did it to protect us
and the good of the nation.

238
00:12:59,480 --> 00:13:02,897
Yeah, well, that may be true, but
I didn't want anyone to get hurt.

239
00:13:02,980 --> 00:13:05,097
Oh, no, you don't have
to worry about that.

240
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:08,457
Apparently, the facilities that
got destroyed were mana furnaces.

241
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:10,080
Mana furnaces? Yes.

242
00:13:10,480 --> 00:13:13,480
Those areas have a very
high concentration of mana,

243
00:13:13,620 --> 00:13:15,437
so people aren't able to enter them.

244
00:13:15,520 --> 00:13:16,500
Oh, yeah?

245
00:13:16,880 --> 00:13:18,409
Then that's good, I guess.

246
00:13:18,520 --> 00:13:22,377
But of course, it will still affect
the lives of the citizens here.

247
00:13:22,460 --> 00:13:25,284
But not so much that they
can't recover from it.

248
00:13:28,820 --> 00:13:29,650
Brother!

249
00:13:33,700 --> 00:13:36,720
Ben, it's all over now, right? Yes, it is.

250
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:40,437
And we're all moving towards
coordinating post-war reconstruction.

251
00:13:40,520 --> 00:13:44,257
Wait, the war barely started and now
you're telling us that it's already over?

252
00:13:44,340 --> 00:13:49,046
Now I really don't understand why we just
didn't talk it out from the beginning.

253
00:13:50,380 --> 00:13:52,321
So, uh, what about the old fella?

254
00:13:52,460 --> 00:13:53,480
The emperor guy?

255
00:13:53,680 --> 00:13:56,377
He chose to step down
and abdicate the throne.

256
00:13:56,460 --> 00:14:00,813
It is most likely his grandchild will
be chosen to inherit the crown next.

257
00:14:00,980 --> 00:14:02,039
Like a little kid?

258
00:14:02,340 --> 00:14:04,752
They are but ten years old at this point,

259
00:14:04,840 --> 00:14:07,664
which means that a guardian
has to be appointed.

260
00:14:08,160 --> 00:14:09,866
From the ten you met earlier.

261
00:14:10,100 --> 00:14:11,688
Those guys are gonna do it?

262
00:14:12,220 --> 00:14:15,420
